            <p>Generalized anxiety can fragment sustained attention during worry spirals; PTSD intrusive symptoms may interrupt concentration abruptly; depression can blunt initiation energy in ways that resemble procrastination. Medical contributors—including iron deficiency anemia, hypothyroidism, untreated obstructive sleep apnea, untreated hearing loss, medication side effects, and substance rebound effects—sometimes explain attention complaints partly or fully. Californians juggling commutes, housing stress, caregiver demands, unpredictable shift schedules, climate-related disruptions, or seismic routine shocks may describe symptoms escalating sharply—even when the underlying puzzle is burnout or sleep deprivation rather than ADHD.</p>

